# Contributing

If you would like to contribute to this project, please follow these steps:

1. Fork the repository
2. Create a new branch (`git checkout -b feature/branch-name`)
3. Make changes
4. Commit your changes (`git commit -am 'Add some feature'`)
5. Push to the branch (`git push origin feature/branch-name`)
6. Create a Pull Request

## Development environment

After cloning the repository, the development environment can be set up with uv:

```bash
uv sync
# or explicitly:
# uv venv
# uv sync
```

Optionally, the virtual environment can be activated with:

```bash
. .venv/bin/activate
```

## Pre-commit hooks

This project uses [prek](https://github.com/j178/prek) to manage its Git hooks. Prek can be installed via:

```bash
uv tool install prek
```

The Git hooks can be installed by running:

```bash
prek install
```

Prek hooks are defined in [`.pre-commit-config.yaml`](.pre-commit-config.yaml).

## Type checking

This project uses [ty](https://docs.astral.sh/ty/) for type checking. It is installed automatically when setting up the environment with `uv sync`.

## Testing

### Unit tests

To run unit tests locally, use the following command:

```
uv run pytest --inline-snapshot=review

# omit --inline-snapshot option if running headless (CI/Agent):
# uv run pytest
```

### Integration tests

To run tests locally, just run the script `ci/run_testsuite_and_record_V2.sh` from anywhere. The only prerequisite is a working installation of docker or podman.

## Publishing

Publishing new versions is automatically handled by GitHub actions for versions tagged with `x.y.z[.prerelease]` (`1.2.3`, `1.2.3.rc1`, etc.). If you are a maintainer, you can create a new release by following these steps:

1. Switch to the `master` branch:

    ```bash
    git checkout master
    ```

2. Create a new tag:

    ```bash
    git tag 1.2.3
    ```

3. Push the tag to the upstream repository:

    ```bash
    git push upstream 1.2.3
    ```

    To push a tag together with a new commit:

    ```bash
    git push upstream master --tags
    ```
